    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Forty Licks is the Rolling Stones’ career-spanning compilation, first issued in 2002 and designed as a 40-track survey of the band’s remarkable run from the early 1960s through the modern era. It stands out for uniting material from both the ABKCO-controlled Decca/London years and the later Rolling Stones Records catalog, giving listeners a rare, sweeping overview of the group’s evolution from raw blues-rock upstarts to stadium-sized rock icons.\n\nThis 2026 4LP colored-vinyl reissue presents the set in a more deluxe, collectible format, with the full compilation spread across four discs and housed in a gatefold package. Musically, it moves fluidly through signature Stones essentials, balancing the grit of the early hits with later classics and a handful of then-new tracks that underscored the band’s continuing relevance. As a best-of collection, it remains one of the most comprehensive and accessible introductions to the Rolling Stones’ legacy.",
